' startup.vbs.example — template for shell:startup (runs at login, no visible window)
'
' HOW TO USE:
'   1. Copy this file, rename it to something like  my-startup.vbs
'   2. Edit the CurrentDirectory and the Run command below.
'   3. Press Win+R, type  shell:startup  , press Enter.
'   4. Drop your .vbs into that folder. NEVER put a .bat there directly.
'
' The window style 0 = the window is never shown; False = do not wait (the VBS exits immediately
' and your program keeps running in the background).

Dim objShell
Set objShell = CreateObject("WScript.Shell")

' --- edit these two lines ---
objShell.CurrentDirectory = "C:\path\to\your\project"
objShell.Run "cmd /c your-script.bat", 0, False

' Examples of other things you might launch in the background instead:
'   objShell.Run """C:\path\to\pythonw.exe"" ""C:\path\to\your\script.py""", 0, False
'   objShell.Run "cmd /c node server.js", 0, False
